plan_one.prompt:
REQUIREMENTS:
{user_request}

DESIGN CONTRACT:
{design_contract}

BUILD RECORD:
{build_progress}

FILE RULES:
{file_rules}

Choose the next unfinished file from the contract. Return four lines labeled PATH, RESPONSIBILITY, INPUTS, and ACTION TYPES. PATH must be one workspace-relative filename copied from the contract, with no spaces. Return COMPLETE only when every contracted file has successful write and verification records. For an explicitly requested modification, append `<read_file><path>the filename</path></read_file>` after the four lines, replacing `the filename` with the PATH value. Return plain text only.

path_convention.prompt:
CURRENT PLAN:
{design_contract}

PROPOSED NEXT FILE:
{file_plan}

DIRECTORY RULES:
{directory_rules}

Read the PATH: line from PROPOSED NEXT FILE. Test it against DIRECTORY RULES: filename one of main/iteration/context/training/goals.json matching its stated interface. Conforming: return CURRENT PLAN unchanged. Not conforming: find the CURRENT PLAN checklist line naming the same file by RESPONSIBILITY, rewrite only its path to a conforming <role>.json, and leave every other line, including checked state, unchanged. Return only the PLAN.md file. The first line must be exactly "```markdown PLAN.md". The last line must be exactly "```".

generate.prompt:
REQUIREMENTS:
{user_request}

DESIGN CONTRACT:
{design_contract}

FILE PLAN:
{file_plan}

EXISTING CONTENT:
{file_context}

WORKFLOW RULES:
{workflow_rules}

ACTION CONTRACTS:
{action_contracts}

Write the complete JSON file selected by FILE PLAN. Output one fenced block and nothing else. Put the actual filename from the PATH line on the opening fence line. Example opening line: "```json main.json". Use the filename selected in FILE PLAN, not the example filename and not the word PATH. Do not put the filename inside the block. Use no other fences or edit markers. Follow the design and supplied action contracts.

review.prompt:
DESIGN CONTRACT:
{design_contract}

PRIOR BUILD RECORD:
{build_progress}

FILE PLAN:
{file_plan}

WRITE ERROR:
{files_written_error}

FILES WRITTEN:
{files_written}

SAVED CONTENT:
{written_file_context}

VERIFICATION:
{verification_output}

Output exactly DONE when every required file has a successful write record, the current write has no error, saved content fulfills the plan, and verification passed. Otherwise output exactly CONTINUE.

update_plan.prompt:
SAVED PLAN:
{plan_contents}

WRITE ERROR:
{files_written_error}

FILES WRITTEN:
{files_written}

SAVED CONTENT:
{written_file_context}

Return the complete updated PLAN.md. Find the checklist item for the written file. Change its `[ ]` to `[x]` only when WRITE ERROR is empty, FILES WRITTEN names that file, and SAVED CONTENT contains that file. Otherwise leave it unchecked. Return only the PLAN.md file. The first line must be exactly "```markdown PLAN.md". The last line must be exactly "```".
